  (text "ROTARY ENCODER  EC11 / ENC1" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 165.1 148.59 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (thickness 0.3) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "577e15c7-8202-5451-8cb0-93ac649fcaa5"))
  (text "LED CHAIN  (9x SK6812MINI-E, level-shifted from GPIO20)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 186.69 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (thickness 0.3) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f3ff4585-da3a-5ddd-9491-763de0fc6ecc"))
  (text "POWER  (JST battery input)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 224.79 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (thickness 0.3) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "089b0f11-47cc-5a0c-85c6-39d8c5a284d6"))
  (text "RGB power budget: 12mA/channel x 3 x 9 LEDs = 324mA at full white. Fed from VSYS, NOT +3V3 -- SK6812MINI-E's own datasheet specs VDD 3.7-5.5V, below what the 3.3V rail can supply. VSYS is the Li-ion cell/USB rail; it can sag below 3.7V well within normal discharge, so the LEDs may misbehave on a low battery even with brightness capped -- a limitation of the part choice, not a defect here." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 17.78 208.28 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) (thickness 0.3) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1faa1322-6f78-586a-a6cb-e3af5f217e49"))
